So in this particular reaction we're
going to go through this and show how

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:21.559
this reaction can be done in two steps.

00:00:22.090 --> 00:00:26.530
So the whole idea of this is we're going
to be cutting an amide into a carboxylic

00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:32.099
acid and an amine for our first step
and then the second step is how will

00:00:32.110 --> 00:00:34.419
one of the products be neutralized.

00:00:34.705 --> 00:00:38.085
Depending on the conditions
set forth in the reaction.

00:00:38.565 --> 00:00:42.385
So if we have an acid in the reaction,
we're going to neutralize the amine.

00:00:42.495 --> 00:00:45.415
If we have a base in the reaction,
we're going to neutralize the

00:00:45.415 --> 00:00:48.145
carboxylic acid that is being created.

00:00:48.504 --> 00:00:50.844
So let's take a look at this and
let's see if we can, we'll go through

00:00:50.845 --> 00:00:53.539
a bunch of different examples and
try to understand it right here.

00:00:53.860 --> 00:00:55.000
Let's go through the steps.

00:00:55.279 --> 00:00:55.300
All

00:01:00.690 --> 00:01:05.519
right, in order to do a hydrolysis in
two steps, the first part has to do with

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:11.305
the name hydrolysis, which if you kind
of break that apart, hydro, Means water

00:01:11.375 --> 00:01:16.925
and lysis means to cut which you commonly
see in a lot of Biological practices

00:01:16.935 --> 00:01:19.004
is that cutting or breaking of things?

00:01:19.425 --> 00:01:20.645
So we're gonna cut it with water.

00:01:20.935 --> 00:01:22.705
So exactly what does that mean?

00:01:22.705 --> 00:01:26.454
So if you think of the structure of water,
what we're gonna be doing is we're gonna

00:01:26.454 --> 00:01:31.055
be looking at an amide right here So
we're gonna be cutting right in between

00:01:31.055 --> 00:01:36.960
the C double bond O and the nitrogen
portion of the amide And what we're going

00:01:36.970 --> 00:01:39.730
to be doing, we're going to be cutting
that with our little water scissors.

00:01:39.730 --> 00:01:44.200
So when we use the blue scissors,
that is referring to using water.

00:01:44.530 --> 00:01:51.000
Now if you think the structure of water
is H2O or HOH, so there's two components

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:52.580
of this that we're going to be adding.

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:57.970
We have the OH part, and then we
have the hydrogen component that

00:01:57.970 --> 00:02:01.780
are going to be used For this
cutting, so one part is going to be

00:02:01.780 --> 00:02:03.980
added to make the carboxylic acid.

00:02:04.350 --> 00:02:07.320
The other part is going to be added
to the amine, to make the amine.

00:02:07.890 --> 00:02:12.439
Now whenever we see this reaction, this
is typically done under heated conditions.

00:02:12.760 --> 00:02:17.109
That's going to be kind of dissolving and
melting this compound and this question

00:02:17.109 --> 00:02:22.100
mark here means that while depending on
if it's an acid or a base, there's going

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:24.320
to be a second step of the reaction.

00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:27.910
So I left it just as a question mark
