an extra hydrogen, which went on

00:05:01.010 --> 00:05:03.950
the lone pairs of the nitrogen atom.

00:05:04.499 --> 00:05:07.690
So that's all we have to do is show
how that one proton gets donated.

00:05:07.700 --> 00:05:10.719
So if you have an acid hydrolysis,
